hadiths[16]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18171","Waki narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays, from al-Mustawrid, brother of Banu Fihr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: This world in comparison to the Hereafter is but like what one of you puts this finger of his into the sea, so let him see with what it returns. And he pointed with the forefinger."
"18172","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, and Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Ismail informed us, from Qays who said: I heard al-Mustawrid, brother of Banu Fihr, say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By Allah, this world in comparison to the Hereafter is but like what one of you puts this finger of his into the sea, so let him see with what it returns, meaning the one next to the thumb."
"18173","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Luhayah informed us, from Yazid ibn Amr, from Abu Abdur-Rahman al-Hubuli, from al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad, Companion of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he performed ablution, wipe between his toe fingers with his little finger."
"18174","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Sulayman narrated to us, Waqqas ibn Rabiah narrated to us, that al-Mustawrid narrated to them that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever eats a meal at the expense of a Muslim man, and once he said a morsel, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will feed him its like from Hell; and whoever clothes himself with a garment at the expense of a Muslim man, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will clothe him its like from Hell; and whoever stands with a Muslim man in a station of show, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will stand him in a station of show on the Day of Resurrection."
"18175","Jafar ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: Ismail narrated to us, from Qays who said: I heard al-Mustawrid, brother of Banu Fihr, say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: By Allah, this world in comparison to the Hereafter is but like what one of you puts his finger into the sea, so let him see with what it returns to him."
"18176","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Mujalid ibn Saeed narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad who said: I was in a company with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he passed a dead kid goat cast aside. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do you see this as worthless to its owners? They said: O Messenger of Allah, it was from its worthlessness that they cast it away. He said: By Him in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, this world is more worthless to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, than this to its owners."
"18177","Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us, from Ismail who said: Qays narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Mustawrid, brother of Banu Fihr, say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By Allah, this world in comparison to the Hereafter is but like what one of you puts his finger into the sea, so let him see with what it returns to him."
"18178","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Ibn Hubayrah and al-Harith ibn Yazid, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Jubayr who said: I heard al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad say: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever is put in charge of a task for us and has no house, let him take a house; or has no wife, let him marry; or has no servant, let him take a servant; or has no mount, let him take a mount; and whoever acquires anything besides that is a defrauder."
"18179","Hasan ibn Musa and Ibn Dawud narrated to us, they said: Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Amr narrated to us, and Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Luhayah informed us, from Yazid ibn Amr al-Maafiri, from Abu Abdur-Rahman al-Hubuli, from al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad, Companion of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he performed ablution, wipe between his toe fingers with his little finger."
"18180","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, he said: Al-Harith ibn Yazid al-Hadrami narrated to us, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Jubayr, that he was in a gathering in which were al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad and Amr ibn Ghaylan ibn Salamah, and he heard al-Mustawrid say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever is put in charge of a task for us and has no wife, let him marry, or no servant, let him take a servant, or no dwelling, let him take a dwelling, or no mount, let him take a mount; so whoever acquires anything besides that is a defrauder or a thief."
"18181","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Yazid and Abdullah ibn Hubayrah, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Jubayr, and mentioned the hadith."
"18182","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Hubayrah narrated to us, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Jubayr who said: I was in a gathering in which were al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad and Amr ibn Ghaylan, and I heard al-Mustawrid say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever is put in charge of a task for us, and mentioned like the hadith of al-Harith."
"18183","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Mujalid narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By Him in whose Hand is my soul, this world in comparison to the Hereafter is but as a man who puts his finger into the sea then brings it back. He said: And I was in the company with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he passed a kid goat cast aside on a dunghill, and said: Do you see this as worthless to its owners? They said: It was from its worthlessness that they cast it here. He said: By Him in whose Hand is my soul, this world is to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, more worthless than this to its owners."
"18184","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abbad ibn Abbad, meaning al-Muhallabi, narrated to us, al-Mujalid ibn Saeed narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: By Allah, this world in comparison to the Hereafter is but as a man who puts his finger into the sea then it returns to him, so what did it take from it. He said: And al-Mustawrid said: I bear witness that I was with the company who were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he passed the dwelling of a people who had departed from it, and behold a kid goat thrown aside. So he said: Do you see this as worthless to its owners when they cast it away? They said: It was from its worthlessness to them that they cast it away. He said: By Allah, this world is more worthless to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, than this to its owners."
"18185","Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Layth ibn Saad narrated to us, Musa ibn Ali narrated to us, from his father, from al-Mustawrid al-Fihri, that he said to Amr ibn al-As: The Hour will come while the Romans are the majority of people. So Amr ibn al-As said to him: Watch what you say. He said: I tell you what I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So Amr ibn al-As said: If you have said that, they have four qualities: They are the swiftest of people to rally after a rout, they are the best of people to the poor, the needy and the weak, they are the most forbearing of people at tribulation, and the fourth is a good and beautiful one: They are the most resistant of people to the oppression of kings."
"18186","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Jubayr, that al-Mustawrid said: While I was with Amr ibn al-As, I said to him: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The Romans will be the severest of people against you, and their destruction will be with the Hour. So Amr said to him: Did I not forbid you from the like of this."
